{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThere is a latent 4-hop import cycle in `src/rebar/llm/`, held open only by two deferred\n(function-body) imports:\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py:38` — `from rebar.llm.completion import\n   verify_step_floor` — module level\n2. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:43` — `from . import completion_banking as\n   _bank` — module level\n3. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:684` — `from .completion_recovery import\n   CompletionAgentStep, raise_completion_workflow_failure` — inside a function\n4. `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:446` — `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` —\n   inside a function\n\n`verify_step_floor` (`completion.py:235`) is a ~15-line arithmetic clamp over a `VerifyConfig`\n(criteria count + direct-child count + 4 config fields -> an int). It is the only reason\n`completion_banking.py` needs a module-level edge back into `completion.py`. Both deferred\nimports are unmarked as cycle-breakers — tidying up either one (an ordinary refactor move)\nsilently breaks the package import at runtime. That invisibility, not the cycle itself, is the\ncost: nothing flags these two imports as load-bearing.\n\n**Verified by execution on `origin/main@2e28d817a7eefca3935a0ead4c84d584eda8c201`** (not by\nreading): copied `src/` to scratch, used an `ast`-based hoist (parses the module to find the\ntrue end-of-import-block line, past the docstring, so the inserted statement never lands inside\na parenthesized import) to move imports 3 and 4 to module level, then imported:\n\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'verify_step_floor' from partially initialized module\n'rebar.llm.completion' (most likely due to a circular import)\n  .../workflow/completion_recovery.py, in <module>: from . import completion_banking as _bank\n  .../workflow/completion_banking.py, in <module>: from rebar.llm.completion import verify_step_floor\n```\n\nHoisting import 4 alone imports cleanly — confirming import 4 alone does not close the loop;\nboth hoisted together reproduces the cycle.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove `verify_step_floor` and its constant `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` (`completion.py:67`) into\n`src/rebar/llm/config.py`. `config.py` is the right home: the function's only non-literal input\nis a `VerifyConfig`, so the clamp is a config-driven computation, and `config.py` does not\nimport `completion.py` (direct or transitive — confirmed by reading its import block), so the\nmove cannot recreate the cycle. `config.py` is 553 LOC; the move adds ~23 LOC, landing at ~576\n— under the 800 cap, above the 200-500 target band (noted; splitting `config.py` is out of\nscope here).\n\n`completion.py` re-imports `verify_step_floor` from `rebar.llm.config` at module level (joining\nthe existing `from rebar.llm.config import VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL, LLMConfig` line) so its own\ncall site (`:433`) still works and `completion.verify_step_floor` stays a resolvable module\nattribute for the existing `monkeypatch.setattr(completion, \"verify_step_floor\", ...)` test\nseam. `completion_banking.py:38` re-points to `rebar.llm.config`. With that edge gone, imports 3\nand 4 both become ordinary module-level imports.\n\n**Verified by execution:** applied this move in the scratch copy, re-hoisted both edges, and\n`import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm` succeeded. A\nwhole-tree `pkgutil.walk_packages` sweep over `rebar.*` found the same 2 pre-existing failures\nas the unmodified tree (`rebar.opcert_service.app`, `rebar.review_bot.app`, both\n`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fastapi'` — not installed in this venv). No new failure,\nno new cycle.\n\nThis moves **one function** to close **one cycle** — it does NOT hoist the ~258 other lazy\nimports across `llm/`. A prior review tested that broader move: hoisting generally binds the\nimported name at load time, so a later `monkeypatch.setattr` on the *original* source module (the\nmajority object-form pattern among the suite's ~2,900 patch sites, vs. the minority\n`importlib`/string-form) stops reaching the call site — 4 regression files / 6 failing tests,\nrefuted. This ticket touches exactly the two edges whose cycle was reproduced above, and\nverifies each existing patch seam individually (see Testing).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion.py` — remove `verify_step_floor` (`:235`) and\n  `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` (`:67`); add `verify_step_floor` to the existing config import line;\n  hoist `from rebar.llm.workflow import gate_dispatch` (`:446`) to module level.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — add `verify_step_floor` + `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` (moved\n  verbatim with their docstring/comment).\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py` — re-point `:38`'s import to `rebar.llm.config`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — hoist the `completion_recovery` import (`:684`)\n  to module level.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py` — re-point `:20`'s import to\n  `rebar.llm.config`.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_verdict_cache.py` — re-point the `:549` in-test import\n  to `rebar.llm.config`.\n- `tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py` — no code change expected at\n  `:455` (the `monkeypatch.setattr(completion, \"verify_step_floor\", ...)` seam survives via the\n  re-import); verified by running the test, not by inspection alone.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run the 3 directly affected test files and confirm all pass — the exhaustive set of\n  non-source references to the moved symbols (confirmed by `grep -rn \"verify_step_floor\\|\n  _VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX\" src tests docs`).\n- Confirm `python -c \"import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm\"`\n  succeeds with both lazy imports hoisted to module level — the regression check for the cycle\n  this ticket closes.\n- Run `make verify` (lint + typecheck + import-convention guard + the full `not integration and\n  not external` suite) and confirm it passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `verify_step_floor` / `_VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX` are defined in `src/rebar/llm/config.py`\n      and no longer in `completion.py`; checked by `grep -n \"def verify_step_floor\"` against\n      each file (1 hit in `config.py`, 0 in `completion.py`).\n- [ ] `gate_dispatch.py`'s `completion_recovery` import and `completion.py`'s `gate_dispatch`\n      import are both module-level (not inside a function body); checked by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import rebar.llm.completion, rebar.llm.workflow.gate_dispatch, rebar.llm\"`\n      exits 0 from the worktree root with the venv active.\n- [ ] The 3 affected test files pass under the bare `pytest` console script.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes (lint, typecheck, import-convention guard, full suite).\n- [ ] No file in `src/rebar` exceeds 800 LOC after the change (checked by `wc -l\n      src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/completion.py`; expected ~576 / ~452 LOC).\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793821806986674197,"uuid":"438f4271-e310-48e7-9732-04efb578b534"}